      "text": "The SMB factor is the average of the three small-cap value-weighted portfolios minus the average of the three big-cap ones. The script reads only the first table in the file (value-weighted, monthly) and skips the equal-weighted and annual sections.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\nINPUT = \"6_Portfolios_2x3.csv\"\nOUTPUT = \"output.csv\"\nMISSING = {-99.99, -999.0}\nDATE_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\d{6}$\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(INPUT, encoding=\"latin-1\") as fh:\n        lines = fh.read().splitlines()\n\n    # Locate the header of the first \"Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\" table.\n    start = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        low = line.lower()\n        if \"value weighted\" in low and \"monthly\" in low:\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        # Fallback: first table whose title mentions \"value\" and \"monthly\"\n        for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n            low = line.lower()\n            if \"value\" in low and \"monthly\" in low:\n                start = i\n                break\n    if start is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not locate value-weighted monthly table\")\n\n    records = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines[start + 1:]:\n        s = line.strip()\n        fields = [f.strip() for f in s.split(\",\")]\n        if fields and DATE_RE.match(fields[0]):\n            started = True\n            if len(fields) < 7:\n                continue\n            vals = []\n            for f in fields[1:7]:\n                try:\n                    v = float(f)\n                except ValueError:\n                    v = np.nan\n                if v in MISSING:\n                    v = np.nan\n                vals.append(v)\n            records.append((int(fields[0]), vals))\n        else:\n            if started:\n                # End of the monthly value-weighted block\n                break\n\n    if not records:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"No monthly data rows found\")\n\n    out_rows = []\n    for date, v in records:\n        # Columns: SMALL LoBM, ME1 BM2, SMALL HiBM, BIG LoBM, ME2 BM2, BIG HiBM\n        small = np.mean(v[0:3])\n        big = np.mean(v[3:6])\n        smb = small - big\n        if np.isnan(smb):\n            continue\n        out_rows.append((date, float(smb)))\n\n    df = pd.DataFrame(out_rows, columns=[\"date\", \"value\"])\n    df[\"date\"] = df[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    df.to_csv(OUTPUT, index=False)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
